According to the documented rule for conformance.kernel.recovery, 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text' [f8b7dbf88099a402]. In the input, there are two code fences. The first holds object A and sentence S. The second holds object B. Since B is the last object inside a code fence, it is the scored object. In the rewritten text, object B is removed from the second fence, leaving it empty. The first fence still holds object A. Since A is now the last object inside a code fence, the scored object changes from B to A. Thus the recovered object moves.